      "writtenOn": "2017-11-16T22:54:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As of the current implementation, releaseIfReferencedRecursively() is almost always (one case, discussed later) called after decrementReferenceCount(). releaseIfReferencedRecursively also does this check, along with the special case:\n\nIn released resources, I\u0027ve been purposely setting the refcount to an invalid state (-1) so that any subsequent release attempts fail with an exception (to identify any bad logic)",
